<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH SENATE ELECTIONS RESULTS - ALL DECLARED.</title>
<headline>CZECH SENATE ELECTIONS RESULTS - ALL DECLARED.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are results in the</p>
<p>first round of elections to the new Czech Senate on Saturday</p>
<p>with all 81 constituencies declared.</p>
<p>		  WON    * IN RUNOFF AS  * IN RUNOFF AS</p>
<p>		OUTRIGHT * TOP CANDIDATE * 2ND CANDIDATE</p>
<p>    ODS	  3     *     73	  *	3</p>
<p>    CSSD	 0     *	0	  *     48</p>
<p>    KDU-CSL    1     *	1	  *     16</p>
<p>    KSCM	 0     *	1	  *	3</p>
<p>    ODA	  0     *	2	  *	5</p>
<p>    OTHERS     0     *	0	  *	2</p>
<p>Note. These figures, from the Czech Elections Commission</p>
<p>(UVK), are provisional until confirmed later in the week.</p>
<p>The parties listed are:</p>
<p> ODS:     CIVIC DEMOCRATIC PARTY</p>
<p> CSSD:    CZECH SOCIAL DEMOCRATIC PARTY</p>
<p> KDU-CSL: CHRISTIAN DEMOCRATIC UNION-CZECH PEOPLE'S PARTY</p>
<p> KSCM:    COMMUNIST PARTY OF BOHEMIA AND MORAVIA</p>
<p> ODA:     CIVIC DEMOCRATIC ALLIANCE</p>
<p>If no candidate receives more than half the vote in a</p>
<p>constituency in the first round, the top two candidates will</p>
<p>meet in a runoff on November 22 and 23.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
